{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25600226",
      "title": "Summary",
      "sourceHash": "50a0167495f421f8725f97888ea661a3acc8a21640c9c0bc8a2749d2139a9868",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.15,
          "end": 5.6,
          "en": "Now that is it for this course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.6,
          "end": 7.45,
          "en": "Was again another long section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.45,
          "end": 11.76,
          "en": "but it was about a super important topic, Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.76,
          "end": 16.01,
          "en": "And you did learn initially how you can set up Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.01,
          "end": 19.04,
          "en": "without React and then how you can set it up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.04,
          "end": 20.77,
          "en": "without Redux Toolkit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.77,
          "end": 24.82,
          "en": "Now Redux Toolkit is amazing and my strong recommendation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.82,
          "end": 27.61,
          "en": "is to use it because as you saw",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.61,
          "end": 29.55,
          "en": "throughout this course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.55,
          "end": 33.07,
          "en": "it's much easier to manage your state and your reducers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.07,
          "end": 35.37,
          "en": "and your actions when using Toolkit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.37,
          "end": 38.747,
          "en": "instead of having to set up everything on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.747,
          "end": 42.61,
          "en": "Still it's important to know what happens behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.61,
          "end": 45.88,
          "en": "which is why I did start without Redux Toolkit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.88,
          "end": 48.8,
          "en": "so that you really know everything about Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.8,
          "end": 51.93,
          "en": "what you need to know and so that you're also able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.93,
          "end": 56.13,
          "en": "to dive into projects that might not be using Redux Toolkit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.13,
          "end": 58.22,
          "en": "but just Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.22,
          "end": 61.42,
          "en": "Now then you learn about these core Redux concepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.42,
          "end": 63.9,
          "en": "and this Redux flow you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.9,
          "end": 68.72,
          "en": "about actions and reducers or this one root reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.72,
          "end": 71.757,
          "en": "and about the fact that Redux has this one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.757,
          "end": 76.09,
          "en": "central data store that we can create this store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.09,
          "end": 79.78,
          "en": "with configure store when using Redux Toolkit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.78,
          "end": 81.57,
          "en": "And that then as an argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.57,
          "end": 85.85,
          "en": "we pass in an object where we assign our route reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.85,
          "end": 89.5,
          "en": "We either point at just one reducer function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.5,
          "end": 92.138,
          "en": "or we set up such a map of reducers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.138,
          "end": 94.68,
          "en": "which are then merged together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.68,
          "end": 98.2,
          "en": "into one big reducer behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.2,
          "end": 100.60499999999999,
          "en": "Now we also learned how we can then use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.60499999999999,
          "end": 104.1,
          "en": "our Redux managed data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.1,
          "end": 106.13,
          "en": "that we can use useSelector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.13,
          "end": 111.02000000000001,
          "en": "in our components to read data from our Redux managed state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.02000000000001,
          "end": 114.06,
          "en": "and that we can use useDispatch to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.06,
          "end": 116.06,
          "en": "to that dispatch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.06,
          "end": 119.15,
          "en": "which we use to dispatch our actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.15,
          "end": 122.33,
          "en": "which then ultimately leads to our Redux state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.33,
          "end": 123.53,
          "en": "being changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.53,
          "end": 126.87,
          "en": "We also learned that we can pass extra data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.87,
          "end": 130.3,
          "en": "to those actions because you often have actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.3,
          "end": 135.3,
          "en": "and reducer function there for which do need extra data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.7,
          "end": 138.64,
          "en": "We also learned how we would connect a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.64,
          "end": 141.2,
          "en": "class-based component to Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.2,
          "end": 143.29,
          "en": "We're not going to use that in this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.29,
          "end": 146.09,
          "en": "and you might not see it too often out there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.09,
          "end": 147.81,
          "en": "but on the other hand, there are a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.81,
          "end": 151.17000000000002,
          "en": "of projects which still only use class based components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.17000000000002,
          "end": 153.5,
          "en": "So that's definitely also something you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.5,
          "end": 154.59300000000002,
          "en": "should be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.61,
          "end": 158.9,
          "en": "And there for now we have a very solid foundation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.9,
          "end": 161.12,
          "en": "when it comes to Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.12,
          "end": 163.26,
          "en": "Redux is an amazing library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.26,
          "end": 166.55,
          "en": "It can replace React context as you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.55,
          "end": 169.82,
          "en": "but it's also not a must use library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.82,
          "end": 174.35,
          "en": "It's always up to you to decide whether for your project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.35,
          "end": 176.57999999999998,
          "en": "you want to go with React context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.57999999999998,
          "end": 178.6,
          "en": "or if you need Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.6,
          "end": 181.76,
          "en": "React context can have certain disadvantages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.76,
          "end": 186.393,
          "en": "as I mentioned, but they might not matter in your project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.393,
          "end": 191.03,
          "en": "You might not see or measure any performance issues",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191.03,
          "end": 195.11,
          "en": "and you might not have a super complex setup and management.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.11,
          "end": 197.97,
          "en": "Then of course, there's nothing wrong with sticking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.97,
          "end": 201.9,
          "en": "to React context, because you must not forget that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.9,
          "end": 206.59,
          "en": "if you use Redux, you do add an extra third party library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.59,
          "end": 208.01,
          "en": "And that of course adds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.01,
          "end": 211.02,
          "en": "up to the overall code of your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.02,
          "end": 214.01,
          "en": "It makes your application bigger.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 214.01,
          "end": 216.23,
          "en": "So Redux is not always better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 216.23,
          "end": 218.071,
          "en": "It can be a decent option and now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 218.071,
          "end": 223.03,
          "en": "you know how it works and when you should maybe consider it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 223.03,
          "end": 226.2,
          "en": "Now we are going to work more with it throughout the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 226.2,
          "end": 228.69,
          "en": "but this is now a solid foundation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 228.69,
          "end": 231.253,
          "en": "which you need as a React developer.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}